rsa — provenance note
=====================

A record only. Nothing in this file imposes a redistribution condition beyond
zig-libs' own MIT license (see the repository `LICENSE`). Moved here from the
root `NOTICE` §2 on 2026-08-14, unchanged in substance.

Clean-room from published specifications; no third-party source copied.

Design references
-----------------

  * RFC 8017 (PKCS #1 v2.2) — RSAEP/RSAVP1/RSADP/RSASP1 primitives,
    EMSA-PKCS1-v1_5, RSAES-OAEP + MGF1, RSASSA-PSS.
  * RFC 5280 (X.509), RFC 5208 (PKCS #8), RFC 7468 (PEM), RFC 4251 §5 (SSH
    string/mpint) — key parsing + certificate.
  * Zig std's internal `std.crypto.Certificate.rsa` (**MIT**) for the
    `Modulus`/`Fe`/`PublicKey` shape only (that struct is not `pub` and is
    verify-only — no `SecretKey`/CRT/signing to copy from).
  * OpenSSH `PROTOCOL.key` (openssh-key-v1 private-key container) — format
    only.
  * B. Schneier, "Description of a New Variable-Length Key, 64-Bit Block
    Cipher (Blowfish)", FSE '93 — Blowfish; the P-array/S-box pi constants
    were independently recomputed, not copied.
  * OpenBSD `bcrypt_pbkdf` (Ted Unangst) — the KDF algorithm, implemented from
    its published description.

Test vectors (validation only, not design)
------------------------------------------

OpenSSL-generated KATs, Eric Young's Blowfish ECB vectors (schneier.com), and
`golang.org/x/crypto` `bcrypt_pbkdf` reference vectors — all cited inline at
their tests.
